module gunbc.plans.ntfy_deployment_gate_approval

// PLAN CARRIER: replacing the GitHub "Review deployments" click with the operator's existing ntfy
// tap, for the fleet-converge jobs that gate behind a deployment environment. Written before any
// implementation PR, because this changes WHAT RELEASES THE srv1 ROOT-MUTATION BOUNDARY — the
// highest-stakes authority question in the repository — and DESIGN.md §3b requires a plan carrier
// naming the invariant, the rejected alternative, and the retirement condition for exactly that
// class of change.
//
// THE OBSERVATION THAT SHAPES THE PLAN (measured, not assumed, on 2026-10-17/18 against
// gunb-ai/gunbc): the operator is NOT currently clicking twice for one decision. `srv1-production`
// is the only environment with RequiredReviewers, it has exactly ONE reviewer (the operator), and
// its gated jobs (dashboard-deploy, approval-broker-dark-install, microvm-controller-install) are
// gated by GitHub ALONE — no ntfy request is filed for them. The two loops already sit on
// DISJOINT jobs: the ntfy loop on gcp-iam-converge and printer (which have no RequiredReviewers at
// all), the GitHub gate on the three srv1 jobs. So the work is not "remove a duplicate authority";
// it is "move the srv1 gate onto the surface the operator already uses". That is a real
// improvement and it is a different, harder thing: it puts a NEW actor in the release path of root
// mutation, and every claim below is written to that bar rather than to the easier story.

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import std.types { List }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn ntfy_deployment_gate_approval_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal/current ruling:** one device approval for srv1 root mutation. SUPERSEDED on 2026-10-26 by gunbc.design_ruling.srv1_root_mutation_approval_is_filed_by_the_job: route B. Each job first files one broker access request and proceeds only on device-redeemed approval through gunbc.fleet.srv1_root_mutation_approval_run. No App answers a deployment protection rule. Keep the environment’s main-only branch rule; the operator removes its required reviewer only after a real dispatch demonstrates both admission and denial. Historical option-A stages 3–5 below are NOT to be executed. Landed stages 1–2 remain until removed with their consumers. This plan enforces nothing."),
    p(text: "**Historical decision/observation:** the 2026-10-18 default approval of option A (msg_4d0c3073, manager warm-crane-219) was not the operator’s personal approval of the root-boundary change; it never authorized lifting DARK or reviewer removal. The 2026-10-17/18 audit found disjoint loops, not duplicate approvals: srv1 dashboard-deploy, approval-broker-dark-install and microvm-controller-install used GitHub only; GCP IAM/branch-run-grant and printer requests used the broker’s single approval_capability_authority (gunbc.auth.scoped_authorization). Run 35447067113 existed and failed, but its reported tap was not verified against tailnet broker state. [Original audit, API readings and stage history](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/ntfy_deployment_gate_approval.dag) are dated evidence, not current deployment claims."),
    p(text: "**Preserved boundaries:** srv1-production keeps its main-only deployment policy, independently of approval mechanism; re-read it after reviewer removal. Keep mtcollins1-boot and its managed_host_boot_federation WIF environment claim. Do not infer a branch policy where the audit found none. can_admins_bypass was true: emergency UI bypass means device-only approval is not an invariant; changing bypass belongs to the operator. The audit’s unresolved mtjade1-arrival/namecheap-dns/printer-lan environment references need a separate work item, not an unreviewed expansion of this boundary change."),
    p(text: "**Rejected alternatives:** notify-only keeps the unwanted click; broker possession of an operator GitHub token or calls to human pending_deployments impersonate the operator and violate authorization_pattern_selection; deleting environments/policies breaks the boundary/federation; publicly exposing the tailnet-only, loopback/Tailscale-served, mTLS-admitted broker for webhooks adds unnecessary authority exposure. These restrictions survive the route change."),
    p(text: "**Retained option-A model contract (historical, not a work order):** extdeps.github.deployment_protection_rule owns requested webhook activity; POST actions/runs/\{run_id\}/deployment_protection_rule with environment_name, approved|rejected, optional comment and exact 204 success; read-only pending_deployments; enabled custom-rule ownership; Deployments:write on an installation token. Apps answer only their own custom rules, never a human reviewer wait. protection_rules’ enum contains required_reviewers, wait_timer and branch_policy, not a fabricated custom-rule arm. A separate least-privilege App was proposed with Actions:read, Deployments:write, event subscription and one-repo installation; its key follows host_secret_custody, never workflow-secret custody. App creation/install/webhook/enablement are FleetOnce human_intervention rows, not agent acts."),
    p(text: "**Timeout evidence:** rule_gate_approval_ceiling and custom_rule_response_timeout are independent Second transcriptions from the limits and custom-rule references; gate_ceilings_agree compares them in both directions. Neither derives from the other. custom_rule_timeout_run_conclusion uses RunFailure; no English “fails” grep or invented JobApproved arm. A hung broker/request leaves the gate waiting until failure. The historical 30-day limit applied to both existing reviewer approvals and custom-rule responses; it was not a new cost introduced by the proposal."),
    p(text: "**Retained verification contract:** option A requires an earlier ungated filing job, since no step behind an environment gate can file a request. It polls to terminal answered/rejected/expired, never leaves a tap dangling. Polling is read-only evidence, not approval. Verify the filed run/environment against pending_deployments, and verify an enabled custom rule’s App id AND slug against the observed installation; PendingDeploymentReviewer only carries User|Team, so a human reviewer does not disqualify a staged trial and current_user_can_approve is not App authority. Mint ObservedRuleOwnership from enabled-rule readback. The outward effect ladder excludes the human review endpoint through broker_barrier_against_the_human_review_endpoint."),
    p(text: "**Capability/request binding:** ApprovalCapabilityClaims carries protocol, issuer, audience, authority, escalation id, revision, decision, attempt and timestamps; it has NO environment field. The filed claim supplies the environment, corroborated by readback. Consume only the approved current single-use revision. Run id is in the URL; environment_name is in the actual sent body, so checking the path alone is insufficient. Refuse unverifiable claims, wrong run, wrong environment, wrong repository, stale revision and expired capability. A rejection has no invented reason: comment is Absent until the typed capability carries one."),
    p(text: "**Retained DARK route:** gunbc.fleet.deployment_gate_answer folds begin→installation→ownership→broker→protection→review_phase into typed stop/next request. Sealed clearance makes review unconstructible while a required reviewer remains. Recorded response binds method, path and actual sent body. test.claim.deployment_gate_answer_witness uses supplied wire facts, not proof of real I/O. A future separately authorized actuator would reuse github_effect_perform/app_jwt_for for reads/token/review, never build a second HTTP path; privileged_effect_census.answer_pending_gate_effect belongs with that real caller, not a false RealizedAuthorization or RealizedUnauthorized row. Its historical polling-versus-webhook divergence must be recorded."),
    p(text: "**Historical trial/removal obligations, dormant under route B:** only an operator-authorized actuator could lift DARK for a non-mutating trial with the reviewer still present. DeploymentGateTrialEvidence must pin real approve AND reject receipts to srv1-production; reviewer-free tests cannot qualify. Exactly 204 from the broker’s actual route proves accepted review, not a supplied or stand-in request. Wrong run/body environment/repository mutations must refuse. Network/403/404/rate-limit/non-204, revoked installation, broker failure, expiry and revision mismatch never become approval or a retry into approval. Failed rejection remains waiting and is distinguished from posted rejection."),
    p(text: "**Historical removal producer contract:** deployment_gate_removal.read_removal_boundary_standing alone consumes the standing mint and read_observed_instant; post-removal readback alone consumes observe_reviewer_removal, apart from confined fixtures. One owner/repo/environment value MUST address every environment/install read and supply GateSubject to the mints; separate caller-authored matching labels make the join decorative. No fabricated owner/repo/url fields in GitHub’s environment response. Sealed observations join exact environment protection and rule ownership; standing is boundary-, attempt- and age-bound with standing_max_age/reason. Refuse wrong attempt/boundary/stale standing. GitHub has no protection CAS, so the read→human-act window remains explicit. Re-read main-only policy after removal. The unchanged retirement metadata below records the superseded option-A contract; it does not override the current route-B ruling."),
  ]
}

data ntfy_deployment_gate_approval_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "ntfy-deployment-gate-approval",
  title: "Approve GitHub deployment gates from ntfy: what actually gates srv1 today, and the staged swap that keeps the boundary closed",
  body: ntfy_deployment_gate_approval_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen {
    condition: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "Delete this record when the rows it asks for are in the tree and enforce what they claim: extdeps.github.deployment_protection_rule is rostered and cited with its discriminating witness green by execution; gunbc.auth.authorization_pattern_selection carries the selected App-rule pattern and the excluded operator-token / broker-calls-human-reviewer / notify-only patterns for the effect 'answer a pending environment gate for a run'; std.human_intervention FleetOnce rows exist for the App creation, installation and per-environment rule enablement; the broker's review call is witnessed with 204 on the real route for BOTH approved and rejected on a real dispatch; the removal act is issued only against a standing read FRESH for the attempt that asks for it — bounded and attempt-bound, which is what is actually true: the standing is sealed and carries the boundary, the observation attempt and the instant it was read, so an act refuses a standing for another attempt or another boundary, and one older than a declared age bound (standing_max_age) with a stated reason. Its two protection facts (the human required-reviewer still present, the main-only branch rule still present) are joined to the rule-ownership read through a sealed environment-protection observation, minted only from the exact GET .../environments/\{environment_name\} readback, so a sibling environment's healthy protection cannot be joined to srv1's ownership. WHAT CANNOT BE MODELED, and is declared as a residual rather than papered over: GitHub offers no compare-and-set on environment protection and a human clicks after the read, so there is an observation-to-action window that no model can close; srv1-production's main-only branch policy has been re-read after the required-reviewer removal; and the mutated-binding reds (wrong run id, wrong environment, and the same pair witnessed on another REPOSITORY) are shown not to approve. Until every one holds, this carrier is the only place the measured gate state, the rejected alternatives and the stage gate are written down.",
    ),
  },
}
